---
/**
 * Terms for the hosted beta at micaforge.com, and the plain-language reading of
 * the software licence for everyone who runs Micaforge themselves.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { IconOut } from "../components/react/icons.tsx";

const sections = [
  { id: "who", t: "1. Who we are" },
  { id: "beta", t: "2. The beta" },
  { id: "account", t: "3. Your account" },
  { id: "use", t: "4. Acceptable use" },
  { id: "data", t: "5. Your data" },
  { id: "visitors", t: "6. Your visitors" },
  { id: "licence", t: "7. The software licence" },
  { id: "warranty", t: "8. No warranty" },
  { id: "liability", t: "9. Liability" },
  { id: "ending", t: "10. Ending" },
  { id: "changes", t: "11. Changes to these terms" },
  { id: "law", t: "12. Disputes" },
  { id: "contact", t: "13. Contact" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Terms · Micaforge"
  description="Terms for the free Micaforge hosted beta at micaforge.com, and what the AGPL-3.0 licence means if you run Micaforge yourself."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main">
    <article class="mf-wrap mf-doc">
      <header class="mf-doc__head">
        <h1 class="mf-doc__title">Terms</h1>
        <p class="mf-doc__lede">
          These terms cover the hosted beta at micaforge.com. If you run Micaforge on your own
          server, only the software licence in section 7 applies to you.
        </p>
        <div class="mf-doc__meta">
          <span>Last changed <strong>8 October 2026</strong></span>
          <span><strong>AGPL-3.0</strong> server · <strong>MIT</strong> tracker and SDK</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <nav class="mf-toc" aria-label="Contents">
        <ol>
          {sections.map((s) => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.t}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <Prose class="lg-body" as="section">
        <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          The hosted service at micaforge.com is operated by{" "}
          <strong>Internet Technology Services LLC</strong> (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;).
          By creating an account you agree to these terms.
        </p>

        <h2 id="beta">2. The beta</h2>
        <p>
          The hosted service is in beta and free of charge. Features can change, and the service
          can be unavailable while we work on it. We do not promise any uptime or response time
          during the beta. To keep the service usable for everyone, we may limit how many sites or
          organisations one account has.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we introduce paid plans, we will tell you by email at least 30 days before any charge
          could apply, and nothing will be charged without your agreement.
        </p>

        <h2 id="account">3. Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You sign in with a one-time code we send to your email address. There is no password.
          Keep access to that mailbox secure, because whoever controls it can sign in to your
          account. You are responsible for what happens in your account and for the people you
          invite to your organisations.
        </p>

        <h2 id="use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Measure only sites you own or are allowed to measure.</li>
          <li>Use the service lawfully, and do not use it to collect data you have no right to collect.</li>
          <li>Do not try to break, overload or get around the limits of the service, or reach data that is not yours.</li>
          <li>Do not send traffic that is not real visitor or crawler activity on your sites.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="data">5. Your data</h2>
        <p>
          The analytics data your sites send belongs to you. We process it only to run the service
          for you, as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and the{" "}
          <a href="/dpa">data processing terms</a>. We do not sell it, and we do not use it to
          advertise to anyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can export your data as CSV at any time. Deleting a site removes it at once; its event
          rows are removed by the next cleanup run. To delete your account, write to us.
        </p>

        <h2 id="visitors">6. Your visitors</h2>
        <p>
          Micaforge is designed to measure traffic without cookies and without personal data. You
          are still the one who decides to measure your sites, so you are responsible for your own
          privacy notice and for the law that applies to your visitors.
        </p>

        <h2 id="licence">7. The software licence</h2>
        <p>
          The server and the dashboard are licensed under the{" "}
          <strong>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3</strong>. The browser tracker and the
          SDK packages are licensed under the <strong>MIT licence</strong>, so embedding them in your
          pages does not affect your own code.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may run Micaforge yourself for any purpose. If you <strong>modify</strong> it and let
          other people use your modified version <strong>over a network</strong>, you must offer them
          the source of your version. Running it unmodified, or modifying it for your own use, is not
          affected.
        </p>
        <p>
          The licence covers the code, not the name. You may say a product is built on Micaforge or
          is a fork of it, but do not name a fork in a way that suggests it is this project.
        </p>

        <h2 id="warranty">8. No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The service and the software are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;, without warranty of any kind,
          express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
          non-infringement.
        </p>

        <h2 id="liability">9. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Internet Technology Services LLC is not liable for
          any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for any loss of
          profits, revenue, data or goodwill, that results from your use of the service, from being
          unable to use it, or from an interruption or end of the service. Nothing in these terms
          limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ending">10. Ending</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using the service at any time. We may suspend or close an account that breaks
          these terms. If we end the beta or the hosted service, we will give you at least 30 days'
          notice by email so you can export your data or move to a self-hosted install, which runs
          the same software.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          If we change these terms in a way that matters, we will update the date at the top and
          tell account holders by email before the change applies.
        </p>

        <h2 id="law">12. Disputes</h2>
        <p>
          If something goes wrong, write to us first and we will try to resolve it in good faith.
          These terms are governed by applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Internet Technology Services LLC</strong><br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:contact@micaforge.com">contact@micaforge.com</a>
        </p>
      </Prose>

      <div class="mf-next">
        <a class="mf-link" href="https://github.com/loruorg/micaforge/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener">
          The AGPL-3.0 text<IconOut size={13} />
        </a>
        <a class="mf-link" href="/privacy">Privacy<IconOut size={13} /></a>
        <a class="mf-link" href="/dpa">Data processing<IconOut size={13} /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .lg-body { margin-top: var(--mf-12); }
</style>
